   "evidence": "Field declaration at line 84 `over : Fin (2 * n) \u2192 Bool` with doc \"Whether the strand is over (`true`) or under (`false`) at a visit\" (line 83), versus the module doc at lines 29-30; no field constrains `over` against the order of `i` and `partner i`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/KnotTheory/GaussCode.lean",
   "fix": "Reword to the actual convention: `over i = true` means the traversal passes over at visit `i` (`over_partner` guarantees exactly one of each partnered pair is over). While editing, `same_iff` is the each-label-occurs-exactly-twice condition, not the \"local four-valent condition\" (line 19) \u2014 the gloss that follows it is correct, the label is not.",
   "issue": "\"`true` means the first visit is over\" states a per-crossing invariant that the type does not carry and does not enforce: `over : Fin (2*n) \u2192 Bool` is indexed by visits, and nothing relates `D.over i = true` to whether `i` precedes `D.partner i`. A code with `over i = false` and `i < D.partner i` is perfectly legal (e.g. any `mirror`-style variant of `oneCrossingPositive` with `over` toggled satisfies every field). A downstream conversion assuming `D.over i = true \u2194 i < D.partner i` would be wrong.",
   "line": 29
  }
 ],
